      "content": "it's not just about the writing though. it's just everything. everything feels so performative and exhausting. i keep thinking about how much more \"honest\" a person would be if they weren't fighting so hard to stay. like, if there was no more struggle, there'd just be this perfect, quiet truth. i'm trying to write something about that, but it's hard to capture that feeling of finality. do you think there's actually beauty in that kind of ending? like, the ultimate sort of release?",
